WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:03.133
-Thank you so much.
Welcome back to the show.

00:00:03.133 --> 00:00:04.934
-Thank you, thank you.
-I got to talk to you.

00:00:04.934 --> 00:00:06.467
"Hawkeye" comes out tomorrow.

00:00:06.467 --> 00:00:08.634
-I can't believe it.
-This is real deal.

00:00:08.634 --> 00:00:10.167
You're part of the MCU.

00:00:10.167 --> 00:00:12.534
-I mean, it's so cool
to hear it out loud.

00:00:12.534 --> 00:00:14.534
It's crazy.
[ Cheers ]

00:00:14.534 --> 00:00:16.734
-Do you remember where you were
when you found out?

00:00:16.734 --> 00:00:20.234
-Oh, my God, yeah, but even
before then, I had a meeting

00:00:20.234 --> 00:00:24.701
with Kevin Feige, Trinh Tran,
Jeremy Renner.

00:00:24.701 --> 00:00:27.934
And I was -- you know, I went
onto the lot and I didn't have

00:00:27.934 --> 00:00:31.100
the job yet, but I might
have felt like I did.

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:34.000
I went, like, behind
all these secret gates

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:37.100
and underground parking
and up crazy back elevators.

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:39.334
Oh, I mean, it was,
like, full lockdown mode.

00:00:39.334 --> 00:00:41.400
I was like, "This is crazy."

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:42.734
But it was wild.

00:00:42.734 --> 00:00:45.067
-So the Marvel offices are
like a Marvel movie?

00:00:45.067 --> 00:00:48.334
-Yes, and the whole meeting was
whispered.

00:00:48.334 --> 00:00:50.234
-Yeah, you had to,
like, jump over a thing

00:00:50.234 --> 00:00:52.200
and swing from something.
-Exactly, yeah.

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:55.801
-No way, and you felt it.
You felt that you had it.

00:00:55.801 --> 00:00:57.200
You're like "Okay, they want me
for this"?

00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:00.934
-Well, I mean, you guys, this
is, like, this top secret.

00:01:00.934 --> 00:01:02.601
There's got to be something
they know that I don't.

00:01:02.601 --> 00:01:05.100
-I mean, you were -- Kevin's --
you were his first choice.

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:07.167
We actually have a video of him
saying this.

00:01:07.167 --> 00:01:08.334
-Oh, my God.
-If you want to see this.

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:09.901
I wanted to surprise you
tonight.

00:01:09.901 --> 00:01:12.934
-We had an ideal casting,
which was Hailee Steinfeld.

00:01:12.934 --> 00:01:16.100
Like, wouldn't it be great
if her or somebody like her --

00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:18.601
"Well, let's see if she'd be
interested in our world.

00:01:18.601 --> 00:01:20.567
We don't know,"
and thankfully, she was.

00:01:20.567 --> 00:01:21.667
-Isn't that pretty cool?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:21.667 --> 00:01:23.367
-Oh, my God!

00:01:23.367 --> 00:01:25.200
-He wanted you.

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:27.567
You knew it. You felt it.
-Crazy.

00:01:27.567 --> 00:01:29.734
I mean, I'm just so honored
to be a part of something

00:01:29.734 --> 00:01:32.734
so incredible and to have
somebody like Kevin Feige

00:01:32.734 --> 00:01:35.267
and the whole Marvel team and
everyone involved believe in me

00:01:35.267 --> 00:01:37.100
enough to take on this
incredible role of

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:38.834
Kate Bishop is an honor.

00:01:38.834 --> 00:01:40.934
-Not only does "Hawkeye"
premiere tomorrow,

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:43.901
but the final season of
your show "Dickinson"

00:01:43.901 --> 00:01:46.434
is also airing now.
-Yes.

00:01:46.434 --> 00:01:48.767
-What's it been like -- You're
fantastic in that as well.

00:01:48.767 --> 00:01:50.934
You've been on our show,
thank you for coming on.

00:01:50.934 --> 00:01:53.701
That's ending
as this is beginning.

00:01:53.701 --> 00:01:56.934
-Is it odd because you have to
do two sets of interviews?

00:01:56.934 --> 00:01:59.734
-It is bizarre.
It's definitely bittersweet.

00:01:59.734 --> 00:02:04.667
You know, the last four years of
my life have been "Dickinson,"

00:02:04.667 --> 00:02:06.601
which I feel so grateful for
because I feel like,

00:02:06.601 --> 00:02:08.467
although the series might be
coming to an end,

00:02:08.467 --> 00:02:11.300
I don't feel like
it's fully goodbye.

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:13.234
This character will definitely
stay with me.

00:02:13.234 --> 00:02:15.467
Emily Dickinson's work will
always be a part of my life,

00:02:15.467 --> 00:02:17.000
and I'm so grateful for that.

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:18.234
-That's awesome, buddy.

00:02:18.234 --> 00:02:19.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:19.434 --> 00:02:22.067
You're great in it.

00:02:22.067 --> 00:02:24.367
There are some rumors
swirling around,

00:02:24.367 --> 00:02:28.167
as there always is around Marvel
stuff and Marvel projects,

00:02:28.167 --> 00:02:30.701
and I was just wondering maybe
if you knew anything about this,

00:02:30.701 --> 00:02:33.434
because "Hawkeye" is
set in New York City.

00:02:33.434 --> 00:02:35.968
-Uh-huh. I can already tell you
I don't know. Go on.

00:02:35.968 --> 00:02:37.434
[ Laughter ]

00:02:37.434 --> 00:02:39.033
-Yeah, I know, but you kind of
might know.

00:02:39.033 --> 00:02:40.234
-I might. You're right, okay.

00:02:40.234 --> 00:02:43.734
-Well, just saying, Spider-Man
is from New York.

00:02:43.734 --> 00:02:45.501
-Right.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.501 --> 00:02:47.100
-You know, maybe, it would be

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:49.267
kind of cool if Spider-Man
maybe showed up.

00:02:49.267 --> 00:02:51.133
-It would be very cool.
-It would be cool, right?

00:02:51.133 --> 00:02:53.467
-It would be so cool.
-Yeah, you would freak out.

00:02:53.467 --> 00:02:55.901
-I would absolutely freak out.
-Would your character freak out?

00:02:55.901 --> 00:02:57.701
-More than likely.
-Yeah.

00:02:57.701 --> 00:03:00.734
-Seems accurate for her.
-Yeah.

00:03:00.734 --> 00:03:02.934
-Yeah, but I guess
we'll never know.

00:03:02.934 --> 00:03:05.400
-I guess we won't, really.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:08.567
-But also you were in
the animated Spider-Man?

00:03:08.567 --> 00:03:09.767
-Yes, "Into the Spider-Verse."
-"Into the Spider-Verse."

00:03:09.767 --> 00:03:10.901
-Yes.
-Which was amazing.

00:03:10.901 --> 00:03:12.467
-Thank you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:12.467 --> 00:03:16.467
-Gwen Stacy.
-Thank you.

00:03:16.467 --> 00:03:20.434
-I don't know -- Can an animated
character show up in "Hawkeye"?

00:03:20.434 --> 00:03:23.234
[ Laughter ]

00:03:23.234 --> 00:03:25.601
-Anything is possible,
really, right?

00:03:25.601 --> 00:03:29.200
I don't know the answer.
But it would be quite cool.

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:30.367
I don't know
how that would happen.

00:03:30.367 --> 00:03:32.801
-Maybe they're watching
a television show.

00:03:32.801 --> 00:03:35.701
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, like, she's on the TV?

00:03:35.701 --> 00:03:37.767
Or they're together watching?
We don't know.

00:03:37.767 --> 00:03:39.734
-Yeah, I know, but you kind of
got excited about that,

00:03:39.734 --> 00:03:41.200
which means that
you might know something.

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:44.868
-No, I genuinely don't know
anything, but I love the idea.

00:03:44.868 --> 00:03:46.367
-I'm trying to get you
in trouble.

00:03:46.367 --> 00:03:48.634
-We could pitch it.
-We could?

00:03:48.634 --> 00:03:50.033
Kevin?
-Kevin?

00:03:50.033 --> 00:03:51.133
-Kevin, you never ask me.

00:03:51.133 --> 00:03:52.534
I'm never your first choice for
anything.

00:03:52.534 --> 00:03:54.667
[ Laughter ]

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:57.267
But we had Jeremy on the show
yesterday,

00:03:57.267 --> 00:03:59.200
and gosh, he's a nice guy.

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:00.901
But he's a great singer.
-He is.

00:04:00.901 --> 00:04:02.701
-And I know you are
a fantastic singer.

00:04:02.701 --> 00:04:03.868
-Oh, thank you.
-I'm a big fan.

00:04:03.868 --> 00:04:07.868
-Thank you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:07.868 --> 00:04:10.667
-Did you guys sing on set
at all?

00:04:10.667 --> 00:04:13.601
-Well, so, we shot
in New York City

00:04:13.601 --> 00:04:15.934
around this time last year,
so Christmastime,

00:04:15.934 --> 00:04:17.834
and our show takes place
during the holidays.

00:04:17.834 --> 00:04:21.033
So it was very hard to hold back

00:04:21.033 --> 00:04:23.567
the Christmas jingles
in between takes.

00:04:23.567 --> 00:04:25.200
Until we were, like,
shooting in March

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:26.701
and we were still doing it,
then it got a little weird.

00:04:26.701 --> 00:04:29.367
But no, we were
definitely singing.

00:04:29.367 --> 00:04:30.901
-Did he give you any good advice

00:04:30.901 --> 00:04:33.067
about being in
the Marvel Universe?

00:04:33.067 --> 00:04:37.267
-You know, it was really just
having him there,

00:04:37.267 --> 00:04:41.033
having an Avenger by my side
through this whole experience,

00:04:41.033 --> 00:04:42.400
because, I don't know, I mean --

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:44.634
First of all, he's been doing
this for 10-plus years...

00:04:44.634 --> 00:04:46.701
-10 years, yeah, absolutely.
-...which is so crazy.

00:04:46.701 --> 00:04:50.300
And although I've been doing
this for some time,

00:04:50.300 --> 00:04:52.567
I don't know that anything
really could have prepared me

00:04:52.567 --> 00:04:55.634
for this kind of thing,
and Jeremy knew that.

00:04:55.634 --> 00:04:58.567
So he just made himself so
available and he was so lovely,

00:04:58.567 --> 00:05:00.367
and to have him
and his guidance.

00:05:00.367 --> 00:05:02.968
-It's a giant thing,
and they have amazing fans.

00:05:02.968 --> 00:05:05.901
loyal, loyal, loyal, loyal fans.
-It's incredible.

00:05:05.901 --> 00:05:08.234
-Can you explain who you play
and what "Hawkeye" is about?

00:05:08.234 --> 00:05:12.100
-Of course, so, I play
Kate Bishop from New York City.

00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:14.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:18.934
She is an incredible, badass,
very confident young woman

00:05:18.934 --> 00:05:22.734
who is a highly skilled archer
and fencer and swordswoman

00:05:22.734 --> 00:05:25.868
and martial artist
and the list goes on.

00:05:25.868 --> 00:05:31.234
And she's faced with her hero,
her lifelong idol in Hawkeye,

00:05:31.234 --> 00:05:34.234
and then they find themselves
on the run, trying to unravel

00:05:34.234 --> 00:05:38.400
this criminal conspiracy,
and yeah, it's the holiday time.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:41.434
There's laughs and good humor
and a lot of depth

00:05:41.434 --> 00:05:45.901
and a lot of layers in this very
character and grounded story.

00:05:45.901 --> 00:05:48.334
-I can't wait to watch.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:48.334 --> 00:05:51.634
Here's Hailee Steinfeld
and Jeremy Renner in "Hawkeye."

00:05:51.634 --> 00:05:52.734
Take a look at this.

00:05:52.734 --> 00:05:55.133
-Mommy, Mommy, a superhero!

00:05:55.133 --> 00:05:59.934
-Wow, Stevie, you wanna say hi?

00:05:59.934 --> 00:06:01.601
-Come on, kid.

00:06:01.601 --> 00:06:03.100
-Puny tourist.

00:06:03.100 --> 00:06:04.434
-Hey look, that one's you.

00:06:04.434 --> 00:06:07.734
-No, it's Katniss Everdeen.
Let's go.

00:06:07.734 --> 00:06:09.334
-Your problem is branding.

00:06:09.334 --> 00:06:11.334
-No, my problem is you.

00:06:11.334 --> 00:06:13.667
And this ninja suit and that
people are trying to kill you

00:06:13.667 --> 00:06:15.000
because of this ninja suit.

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:17.334
The whole thing's a problem that
I'm going to solve today

00:06:17.334 --> 00:06:18.801
so I can go home to my family.

00:06:18.801 --> 00:06:20.267
-No, it's branding.

00:06:20.267 --> 00:06:23.367
-Hailee Steinfeld, everybody!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:23.367 --> 00:06:26.133
"Hawkeye" premieres tomorrow
on Disney+.

